{"id":"h20t4","name":"Token Bucket Limiter with Plans","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["plans","requests"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>An API gateway limits its clients with token buckets. <code>plans</code> maps a plan name to <code>[capacity, rate]</code>: a bucket holds at most <code>capacity</code> tokens and gains <code>rate</code> tokens per second (integers). <code>requests</code> is a list of strings sorted by time (integer seconds):</p>\n<ul><li><code>\"t REGISTER client plan\"</code>: creates the client with a <b>full</b> bucket. Returns <code>\"OK\"</code>, or <code>\"EXISTS\"</code> if the client already exists (nothing changes).</li>\n<li><code>\"t CALL client cost\"</code>: the call is accepted if the bucket has at least <code>cost</code> tokens; they are removed and the answer is <code>\"ACCEPT remaining\"</code>. Otherwise the answer is <code>\"REJECT wait\"</code>, where <code>wait</code> is the smallest whole number of seconds after which the bucket would have enough tokens if nothing else happened, or <code>\"REJECT never\"</code> if <code>cost</code> is greater than the capacity or if the plan earns no token (<code>rate</code> = 0). A rejected call removes nothing.</li>\n<li><code>\"t PLAN client plan\"</code>: switches the client to another plan from time <code>t</code>. The tokens earned until <code>t</code> are computed with the old plan, then the bucket keeps its tokens, cut down to the new capacity if needed. Returns the number of tokens after the switch.</li></ul>\n<p>Before any operation on a client at time <code>t</code>, its bucket is refilled: <code>tokens = min(capacity, tokens + (t - last) * rate)</code>, where <code>last</code> is the time of its previous refill (its registration for the first one). An operation on an unknown client returns <code>\"UNKNOWN\"</code>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one string per request.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>plans = {\"free\": [10, 1], \"pro\": [100, 5], \"burst\": [50, 0]}</code></p><p><code>requests = [\"0 REGISTER ana free\", \"0 CALL ana 4\", \"1 CALL ana 7\", \"2 CALL ana 8\", \"5 CALL ana 30\", \"6 PLAN ana pro\", \"6 CALL ana 30\", \"10 CALL ana 30\", \"10 PLAN ana free\", \"11 CALL bob 1\", \"11 REGISTER ana pro\", \"20 PLAN ana burst\", \"30 CALL ana 11\"]</code></p><p>the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"OK\", \"ACCEPT 6\", \"ACCEPT 0\", \"REJECT 7\", \"REJECT never\", \"5\", \"REJECT 5\", \"REJECT 1\", \"10\", \"UNKNOWN\", \"EXISTS\", \"10\", \"REJECT never\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> dictionary plans<br><b>[input]</b> array.string requests<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(plans, requests):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["seau à jetons","recharge en continu","changement de plan","temps d'attente arrondi au-dessus","calcul entier"],"minutes":35,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solution(plans, requests)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Ici, la valeur attendue est une liste : compare ce que tu renvoies à « Expected return value » dans les résultats.</li><li>La comparaison est exacte (même type, mêmes valeurs, même ordre dans une liste), sauf les nombres décimaux, comparés à 0,000001 près.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 9 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"plans":{"free":[10,1],"pro":[100,5],"burst":[50,0]},"requests":["0 REGISTER ana free","0 CALL ana 4","1 CALL ana 7","2 CALL ana 8","5 CALL ana 30","6 PLAN ana pro","6 CALL ana 30","10 CALL ana 30","10 PLAN ana free","11 CALL bob 1","11 REGISTER ana pro","20 PLAN ana burst","30 CALL ana 11"]},"expected":{"value":["OK","ACCEPT 6","ACCEPT 0","REJECT 7","REJECT never","5","REJECT 5","REJECT 1","10","UNKNOWN","EXISTS","10","REJECT never"]}},{"input":{"plans":{"x":[3,2],"y":[0,0]},"requests":["0 REGISTER a x","0 CALL a 3","0 CALL a 3","1 CALL a 3","1 CALL a 0","2 CALL a 3","2 REGISTER b y","3 CALL b 0","3 CALL b 1"]},"expected":{"value":["OK","ACCEPT 0","REJECT 2","REJECT 1","ACCEPT 2","ACCEPT 0","OK","ACCEPT 0","REJECT never"]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}